# Flaws (Unearthed Arcana flaw rules; requires Unearthed Arcana)
# Source: The (mostly) Complete Dragon Magazine Compendium - Feats, Flaws & Styles (compendium pp. 1058-1176).
# DESC ends with the original Dragon Magazine issue and article. SOURCEPAGE = compendium PDF page.
# Prerequisites that could not be expressed as PCGen PRE tags are listed in PRETEXT.

Aligned Devotion	KEY:Flaw ~ Aligned Devotion	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Ability to spontaneously cast cure spells	DESC:Your healing powers are only effective for those whose alignment closely matches yours. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Your spells of the healing subschool have reduced effect on those who do not share your alignment. Those that have exactly the same alignment as you gain full benefit from your healing. Those with an alignment within one step of yours are cured half the normal amount of hit points from your healing spells. Characters with alignments more than one step from yours gain no benefit from your healing at all. Your cure spells still deal full damage to undead. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Arcane Conundrum	KEY:Flaw ~ Arcane Conundrum	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESTAT:1,CHA=10	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	DESC:You are unable to use your inborn magical abilities. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You may never use any spell-like abilities under any circumstances. In addition, you suffer a -2 penalty on saving throws versus spells of the illusion school.
Arcane Fatigue	KEY:Flaw ~ Arcane Fatigue	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0	DESC:Conjuring magical energies is especially draining for you. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Whenever you successfully cast an arcane spell you must immediately make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + spell level). If you fail you become fatigued. If you are fatigued as a result of this flaw, it has no further effect until that condition is removed. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Arcane Parasistes	KEY:Flaw ~ Arcane Parasistes	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0	DESC:Thousands of unseen parasites within your flesh draw upon the arcane power held within every spell you cast. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Every arcane spell you cast has the DC to resist it lowered by 1. These parasites cannot be removed by any mortal means, even by a miracle or wish. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Arcane Performer	KEY:Flaw ~ Arcane Performer	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,TYPE.Perform=1	PRETEXT:Ability to cast arcane spells without preparation	DESC:You depend upon your performance ability to aid in the casting of spells. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:In order to cast any spell, you must succeed at a Perform check (DC 10 + spell level). If you fail, you lose the spell. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Beady Eyes	KEY:Flaw ~ Beady Eyes	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREVARGTEQ:DarkvisionRange,1	DESC:You have narrow beady eyes that do not catch the light as well as they should. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You do not have darkvision: instead you possess low-light vision. In addition, you suffer a -2 penalty on all Search and Spot checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Orc
Beastly	KEY:Flaw ~ Beastly	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Wild Empathy	DESC:You have more in common with beasts than you do with your own race. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You are vulnerable to the following list of spells that affect animals, as well as those which affect your own creature type: animal trance, calm animals, charm animal, dominate animal, hide from animals, hold animal. Additionally, you suffer a -2 penalty on all Charisma-based skill checks except Disguise, Handle Animal, and Use Magic Device Anyone observing your mannerisms who possesses the wild empathy class ability can recognize this flaw immediately. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
Bestial Instinct	KEY:Flaw ~ Bestial Instinct	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You prefer to meet your foes so close that you can smell their blood. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty to hit while using anything other than unarmed strikes or natural weapons. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Blind Rage	KEY:Flaw ~ Blind Rage	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Rage,TYPE.Frenzy	DESC:Your ability to distinguish between friend and foe is limited once you enter a rage. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1169	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You may not end your rage voluntarily. Once you enter a rage, you continue to rage for the entire duration. While in a rage, you must attack a creature every round if able. You can charge or move in order to make the attack, and you may move to attack a foe rather than stay still to attack a friend. If there are no creatures within sight, you attack the nearest breakable object. You may attempt a DC 15 Will save once per round on your turn in order stop attacking an ally. If foes become visible, you may immediately switch targets and engage them. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Brash	KEY:Flaw ~ Brash	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You move about without careful consideration of foes. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|AC|-6	TEMPDESC:Against attacks of opportunity	BENEFIT:You suffer a -6 penalty to your Armor Class against attacks of opportunity. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Bravado	KEY:Flaw ~ Bravado	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are rash in combat, refusing to show weakness by falling back from your enemies' blows. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You may not gain the benefit of any kind of dodge bonuses to your Armor Class. Spells, items, and effects that provide a dodge bonus provide no benefit for you. You cannot use the withdraw action during combat. &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Orc
Cautious	KEY:Flaw ~ Cautious	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are uneasy engaging in behavior that carries a chance of failure. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You must spend twice as long performing any skill that requires an action. For example, deciphering a page of text would take 2 minutes for you instead of 1, while the Concentration skill is not affected by this flaw as it does not require an action. You also suffer a -2 penalty on initiative checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Halfling
Chivalrous Courtesy	KEY:Flaw ~ Chivalrous Courtesy	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LG,NG,CG,LN,LE	DESC:You despise raising your hand against creatures of the opposite gender. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls to hit a creature you can tell is of the opposite gender. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
City Slicker	KEY:Flaw ~ City Slicker	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Survival as a class skill	DESC:Although interested in the natural world, you suffer from a lack of experience in the wilds. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BONUS:SKILL|Handle Animal,Knowledge (Nature),Survival|-4	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on all Handle Animal, Knowledge (nature), and Survival checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Claustrophobia	KEY:Flaw ~ Claustrophobia	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are uncomfortable in enclosed spaces. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You become shaken while in any space where you are within 10 feet of a wall or other solid surface on 2 or more sides, or if the ceiling is less than 10 feet above your head. (Such as while walking down a 20-foot-wide corridor or while you are in any room with a 10-foot-high ceiling.) Spells and effects that remove fear do not remove this condition. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Code of Arms	KEY:Flaw ~ Code of Arms	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LG,NG,CG,LN,LE	DESC:Trained to only kill other armed warriors, you hesitate when attacking unarmed opponents. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPDESC:Attacking an enemy not armed with a melee weapon	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls made against an enemy not armed with a melee weapon. If the enemy uses a natural attack against you, you may then attack it without penalty. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Cold-Blooded	KEY:Flaw ~ Cold-Blooded	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You were raised in the arctic and cannot tolerate heat. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You automatically fail all Fortitude saves made to overcome the effects of high temperatures. Fire-based effects deal an additional 2 points of fire damage to you. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Coward	KEY:Flaw ~ Coward	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:In dangerous circumstances, you are likely to run away. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You automatically fail all saves against fear effects. An ability that makes you immune to fear (such as becoming a 3rd-level paladin) instead grants you a saving throw, but at a -4 penalty on the save. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Curious	KEY:Flaw ~ Curious	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are easily distracted by the sights and sounds around you. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BONUS:SKILL|Listen,Spot|-2	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on Listen and Spot checks. You also suffer a -2 penalty on initiative rolls. &nl;Suggested class/race: Gnome
Divine Gestures	KEY:Flaw ~ Divine Gestures	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Divine=0	DESC:Your religious rites require elaborate gestures that cause you difficulty when casting divine spells while wearing armor or using a shield. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a spell failure chance (due to armor, shields, or anything else which causes arcane spell failure) when casting divine spells, just as if they were arcane spells. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Domain Devotion	KEY:Flaw ~ Domain Devotion	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Access to domains	DESC:You are limited to accessing only one of your deity’s domains. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1170	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You choose and have access to only one of your deity’s domains. You may gain prestige domains from a prestige class as usual. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Elven Pride of Arms	KEY:Flaw ~ Elven Pride of Arms	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Elven blood	DESC:You only consider those weapons designed specifically for use by the noblest of elves to be fit to wield. Using any other object as a weapon is beneath your dignity. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPDESC:Using a weapon other than a longsword, rapier or bow	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls when using a weapon other than a longsword, rapier, or bow (long, short, or composite). Attacks made while fighting unarmed, touch attacks (including ranged touch attacks), or attacks made with natural weaponry also incur this penalty. &nl;Suggested class/race: Elf
Exhausting Rage	KEY:Flaw ~ Exhausting Rage	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Rage,TYPE.Frenzy	DESC:You rage so powerfully that you become exhausted once you calm down. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:When you end your rage, you become exhausted (instead of fatigued) for the duration of the encounter. If you gain the ability to rage tirelessly, as a 17th-level barbarian, you are instead fatigued after a rage. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Foe Specialist	KEY:Flaw ~ Foe Specialist	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREVARGTEQ:FavoredEnemyCount,1	DESC:Your training is so specialized that you have difficulty tracking, predicting, or otherwise interacting with those foes you have not studied in great detail. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-1	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|Bluff,Sense Motive,Spot,Survival|-1	TEMPDESC:Against creatures that aren't your favored enemies	BENEFIT:You suffer a -1 penalty on attack rolls, Bluff, Sense Motive, Spot, and Survival checks made against creatures of any kind that isn't one of your favored enemies. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
Fool	KEY:Flaw ~ Fool	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Bardic Music	DESC:Your excessively lighthearted nature grates on your companions. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You lose the inspire courage, inspire competence, inspire greatness, and inspire heroics bardic music abilities. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Forlorn	KEY:Flaw ~ Forlorn	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Ability to call a familiar	DESC:You lack the ability to summon a creature to do your bidding. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You lose the ability to call a familiar. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Forlorn of Men	KEY:Flaw ~ Forlorn of Men	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are uncomfortable in the presence of humanoids. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You become shaken if there is more than one humanoid within 30 feet of you, including members of your adventuring party or other friends. Spells and effects that remove fear do not remove this condition. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Frail	KEY:Flaw ~ Frail	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	!PRESTAT:1,CON=12	DESC:You become fatigued when your body is assaulted by poison or magic. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Whenever you fail a Fortitude save, you become fatigued, in addition to any other effects you might suffer. This condition lasts until you get 8 hours of complete rest. This flaw applies only once to any given source that requires a Fortitude save. Failing a Fortitude save while fatigued causes you to become exhausted. &nl;Suggested class/race: Elf
Free-Spirited	KEY:Flaw ~ Free-Spirited	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Chaotic alignment	DESC:You seek to live your life freely, unburdened by excessive material possessions. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:The weight of any gear you carry is considered double for the purposes of determining your load. For example, a half-elf with a Strength of 10 and 30 pounds of gear is treated as carrying 60 pounds, which is a medium load. In addition, any armor check penalties you have are also doubled (or tripled, in the case of making a Swim check). &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Elf
Frivoulous Performer	KEY:Flaw ~ Frivoulous Performer	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Bardic knowledge	DESC:Having focused your time on practicing and performing, you have gathered little useful information in your travels. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -10 penalty on all bardic knowledge checks. This penalty does not apply if the relevant knowledge involves the Perform skill in which you have the most ranks. For example, if you have the most ranks in Perform (wind instrument), you may use bardic knowledge without penalty to identify famous wind instruments, to remember facts about famous wind instrument players, or to identify places that make quality wind instruments. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Fussy	KEY:Flaw ~ Fussy	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are uncomfortable ingesting any-thing but a small range of preferred foods and drinks. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1171	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|SAVE|ALL|-4	TEMPDESC:Saves against ingested poisons	BENEFIT:You become sickened (no saving throw allowed) upon ingestion of any sort of potion for the duration of its effect, Potions with an instantaneous duration cause you to be sickened for a period of time equal to the potion's caster level in minutes. You also suffer a -4 penalty on saving throws made against ingested poisons. &nl;Suggested class/race: Elf
Glory-Hound	KEY:Flaw ~ Glory-Hound	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETOTALAB:1	DESC:You have an insatiable desire for glorious combat, fighting recklessly to prove yourself. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|AC|-2	TEMPDESC:In combat until you drop an opponent	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty to AC during combat until you drop an opponent. This penalty does not apply if the combat is against a single opponent. &nl;Suggested class/race: Dwarf
Grudge Keeper	KEY:Flaw ~ Grudge Keeper	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You have an overpowering need for vengeance and have difficulty letting go of grudges. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:if you are damaged in combat, you suffer a -2 penalty on attacks rolls, skill checks, saving throws, and ability checks until you damage the foe who caused you harm. This penalty does not apply if you cannot discern the source of the damage. This penalty disappears when the combat ends. &nl;Suggested class/race: Dwarf
Gullible	KEY:Flaw ~ Gullible	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You believe what you see, and you trust others more than you should. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on saving throws made to resist enchantment and illusion spells and effects. You also suffer a -4 penalty on Sense Motive checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Half-Blood Outcast	KEY:Flaw ~ Half-Blood Outcast	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Half-elf or half-orc	DESC:You despise your nonhuman side. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-2	TEMPBONUS:PC|SAVE|ALL|-2	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|TYPE=Base|-2	TEMPDESC:Within line of sight of an elf or orc (see text)	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on all attack rolls, saving throws, and skill checks when within line of sight of an elf (if you are a half elf) or an orc (if you are a half-orc).\
Hatred	KEY:Flaw ~ Hatred	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREVARGTEQ:FavoredEnemyCount,1	DESC:You are engulfed by a deep hatred of your chosen foes and you become insensibly enraged in their presence. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|AC|-4	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|TYPE=Base|-4	TEMPDESC:A favored enemy is in sight and you aren't in melee with it	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty to your Armor Class and on attack rolls and skill checks whenever you are not engaged in melee combat with a favored enemy and a favored enemy is close enough that you could engage it. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
Haunted	KEY:Flaw ~ Haunted	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0,Divine=0	DESC:You are unable to prevent the occurrence of strange noises in your immediate vicinity. [Dragon #327 (Class Acts - Flaws For Sorcerers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Spontaneous noises sometimes arise in your immediate vicinity. These noises are completely out of your control and cannot be used to communicate or distract other creatures. These sounds cease when you are unconscious, petrified, asleep, or dead. You suffer a -4 penalty on all Listen and Move Silently skill checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Sorcerers
Honor of the Duel	KEY:Flaw ~ Honor of the Duel	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LG,NG,CG,LN,LE	DESC:You strongly believe in one-on-one combat to decide a fight. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You must make a Will save (DC 10 + your level) to attack a creature in a square threatened by one of its other foes. A successful save allows you to attack such a creature, albeit with a -2 penalty on your attack rolls. A failed save prohibits you from attacking that creature. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Honorable Challenge	KEY:Flaw ~ Honorable Challenge	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Lawful alignment	DESC:You only cross arms with foes who willingly engage you. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPDESC:Attacking a creature that hasn't challenged or attacked you	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls against creatures that have not explicitly challenged you or made an attack against you. For the purposes of this feat, an attack against you includes any action that would end an invisibility spell (see page 245 of the Player's Handbook). &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Hot-Blooded	KEY:Flaw ~ Hot-Blooded	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You were raised in the desert and cannot tolerate cold. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You automatically fail all Fortitude saves made to overcome the effects of low temperatures. Cold-based effects deal an additional 2 points of cold damage to you. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Implacable	KEY:Flaw ~ Implacable	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETOTALAB:1	DESC:You refuse to retreat from even the most deadly of confrontations. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-2	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|TYPE=Base|-2	TEMPBONUS:PC|SAVE|ALL|-2	TEMPDESC:For 1 hour after leaving melee	BENEFIT:If you move out of melee combat for any reason, you suffer a -2 penalty on all attack rolls, skill checks, and saving throws for 1 hour. &nl;Suggested class/race: Dwarf
Individualist	KEY:Flaw ~ Individualist	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are committed to a path that requires complete independence from others. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1172	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on all attack rolls made using weapons that you have not personally crafted. In addition, the armor check penalty of any suit of armor you wear that you did not craft increases by +1. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
Insomniac	KEY:Flaw ~ Insomniac	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You have great difficulty achieving a full and restful sleep. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:In order to get a full night of rest you must succeed at a DC 15 Fortitude save. If you are sleeping and a disturbance wakes you during the night, you must make an additional save (at the same DC) to return to sleep. If you fail the Fortitude save you are fatigued when you rise in the morning. If you are fatigued when you try to sleep, you gain a +2 bonus on your save. If you are exhausted, you gain a +6 bonus. Comfortable conditions, such as those found in most inns, grant you a +4 bonus on this save. Poor conditions, such as sleeping on the ground or in armor, give you a -4 penalty on this save. Even if you sleep poorly, you may prepare arcane spells as normal after 8 hours of fitful rest. &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Elf
Light Sensitivity	KEY:Flaw ~ Light Sensitivity	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREVARGTEQ:DarkvisionRange,1	DESC:Accustomed only to the darker places in the world, your eyes open much wider than normal, making it difficult for you to see in bright light, [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You become dazzled in bright sunlight or within the radius of a daylight spell. A dazzled creature takes a -1 penalty on attack rolls, Search checks, and Spot checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Orc
Lightweight	KEY:Flaw ~ Lightweight	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	!PRESTAT:1,CON=14	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Flaw ~ Obese	DESC:You are light for your size. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You have half the base weight of a normal character of your race. Height and weight modifiers are added normally. You suffer a -4 penalty when making or resisting bull rushes, grapples, overruns, or trip attacks. You gain no attack bonus when you charge, but you do suffer the -2 Armor Class penalty and take double damage from weapons set against charges you make. &nl;Normal: Characters receive a +2 bonus on attack rolls when charging. &nl;Suggested class/race: Halfling
Living Faith	KEY:Flaw ~ Living Faith	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.TurnUndead	DESC:Your religious practices give you no special powers over the dead. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You lose the ability to turn or rebuke undead. This does not extend to any other creatures a domain might grant you the ability to turn or rebuke, such as earth elementals for a cleric with the Air domain. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Loner	KEY:Flaw ~ Loner	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Ability to summon a familiar or animal companion	DESC:You do not have the ability to summon a familiar or gain an animal companion. [Dragon #327 (Class Acts - Flaws For Sorcerers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You lose the ability to summon a familiar or gain an animal companion. You never gain the ability to gain a special companion, whether through animal companion, summon familiar, or some other class ability or feat. Possessing multiple classes that would grant you an animal companion or familiar does not negate the effects of this flaw. &nl;Suggested class/race: Sorcerers
Loudmouth	KEY:Flaw ~ Loudmouth	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are a loud, obnoxious, boisterous, and compulsive talker. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Move Silently|-4	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on all Diplomacy and Move Silently checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Love of Nature	KEY:Flaw ~ Love of Nature	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You do not wish harm upon any natural creature. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You must succeed at a DC 12 Will save before you can attack any creature with the animal, plant, or vermin type, or you lose your action. Note that animals, plants, and vermin may attack you without penalty. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Magical Fascination	KEY:Flaw ~ Magical Fascination	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You have a tendency to become fascinated by spells and elaborate magical effects. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-2	TEMPBONUS:PC|SKILL|TYPE=Base|-2	TEMPDESC:In sight of a visible non-instantaneous magical effect	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on attack rolls and skill checks when in sight of a visible magical effect with a duration greater than instantaneous (such as a dancing lights, spiritual weapon, or wall of fire spell). &nl;Suggested class/race: Gnome
Magical Overlord	KEY:Flaw ~ Magical Overlord	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0,Divine=0	DESC:You have difficulty controlling your most powerful magic, being more comfortable with more familiar, lower-level spells. [Dragon #327 (Class Acts - Flaws For Sorcerers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1173	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You must use one spell slot of your highest spell level to cast or prepare a spell of a lower level. This spell slot may be used to cast or prepare any spell of any level lower than your highest level, effectively causing you to lose one of your highest-level spell slots to gain one of a lower level. For example, a 6th-level sorcerer would lose the ability to cast one 3rd-level spell per day, but would gain the ability to cast one additional 0, 1st-, or 2nd-level spell instead. This flaw always affects your highest spell level and changes the spell level it affects as you gain levels. &nl;Suggested class/race: Sorcerers
Material Devotion	KEY:Flaw ~ Material Devotion	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Access to domains	DESC:You are restricted to using magical objects created with your deity’s domains in mind. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You many only use spell-trigger items (wands and staffs) that cast spells on your domain spell lists. Other spell trigger items fail in your hands. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Metal Intolerance	KEY:Flaw ~ Metal Intolerance	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are allergic to metals. [Dragon #324 (Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer an additional point of damage when struck by metal weapons. The natural attacks of inevitables, iron golems, and other creatures composed of metal also deal this additional damage. &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Methodical Magical Methods	KEY:Flaw ~ Methodical Magical Methods	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0,Divine=0	DESC:Your spellcasting methods require a rigid posture that makes you vulnerable to your foes while casting. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You are considered flat-footed with an effective Dexterity of 0 (-5 to AC) on any round in which you cast a spell. You may not cast spells defensively. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Meticulous Performer	KEY:Flaw ~ Meticulous Performer	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Bardic Music	DESC:You get lost in your performances. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Initiating or maintaining any bardic music ability is a full-round action. &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Mounted Warrior	KEY:Flaw ~ Mounted Warrior	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Ride=1	DESC:You only feel comfortable fighting from the saddle. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-2	TEMPDESC:While not riding a mount	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on attack rolls made while not riding a mount. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
No Time for Book Learning	KEY:Flaw ~ No Time for Book Learning	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You put no faith in the written word. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Druids)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You are illiterate. You can never learn to read any language, and you suffer a -2 penalty on all Knowledge checks except Knowledge (nature). &nl;Suggested class/race: Druids
Obese	KEY:Flaw ~ Obese	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESIZELTEQ:S	!PRESTAT:1,DEX=14	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Flaw ~ Lightweight	DESC:Your great bulk can sometimes impede your actions. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You have double the base weight of a character of your race. Height and weight modifiers are added normally. You lose your +1 bonus to Armor Class and on attack rolls, as well as your +4 bonus on Hide checks. You must pay double the cost for armor but not for any magical enhancements the armor might have. Such armor does not weigh half the normal amount. &nl;Normal: Small characters receive a +1 bonus to Artnor Class and on attack rolls, as well as a +4 bonus on Hide checks. Armor for small characters weighs half the normal amount. &nl;Suggested class/race: Halfling
Phantom Sparks	KEY:Flaw ~ Phantom Sparks	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0,Divine=0	DESC:Your body occasionally emits bursts of bright colored light. [Dragon #327 (Class Acts - Flaws For Sorcerers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You spontaneously emit bursts of colored light. These lights are completely out of your control and cannot be used as a light source. They only cease when you are unconscious, petrified, asleep, or dead. You suffer a -4 penalty on all Hide and Spot skill checks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Sorcerers
Ponderous Spellcaster	KEY:Flaw ~ Ponderous Spellcaster	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=0,Divine=0	DESC:Your spells take additional time to cast. [Dragon #326 (Class Acts - Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:The casting time of all your spells are doubled. Spells that normally require a single action to cast require a full-round action to cast instead. Spells that normally require a free action to cast now require a standard action to cast instead. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Pride of Arms	KEY:Flaw ~ Pride of Arms	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREWEAPONPROF:1,TYPE.Martial	DESC:You take great pride in knowing how to use weapons specifically designed for war. You consider all other weapons beneath your station and have allowed your training in them to atrophy. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on all attack rolls made with exotic weapons, simple weapons, unarmed attacks, and touch attacks. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Quarter Elf	KEY:Flaw ~ Quarter Elf	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Elf%	DESC:Elven blood is not particularly strong in your veins and its features are barely noticeable. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1174	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You are not immune to sleep spells and do not gain a racial bonus on saving throws against enchantment spells or effects. You are not considered to have elven blood.
Quick Burning Rage	KEY:Flaw ~ Quick Burning Rage	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Rage,TYPE.Frenzy	DESC:Your rages don't last very long. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Your rage only lasts for a number of rounds equal to your newly improved Constitution modifier. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Restricted Sorcery	KEY:Flaw ~ Restricted Sorcery	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Ability to cast spells without preparation	DESC:Your magical powers manifest within a limited realm of effects. [Dragon #327 (Class Acts - Flaws For Sorcerers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Choose two schools of magic to be your restricted schools. When you select spells to learn, you may not choose spells from these two restricted schools. In addition, you may not use wands or scrolls that cast spells from these restricted schools. You may not choose divination as one of your restricted schools. &nl;Suggested class/race: Sorcerers
Short Attention Span	KEY:Flaw ~ Short Attention Span	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You have little patience, causing you to have difficulty concentrating on repetitive tasks. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -2 penalty on all skill checks made to retry an action that you previously failed. This penalty is cumulative, increasing by -2 for every failed attempt. In addition, you may not take 20 on any skill check. &nl;Suggested class/race: Gnome
Short Temper	KEY:Flaw ~ Short Temper	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You become angry and flustered under stressful circumstances. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|AC|-2	TEMPDESC:While enraged	BENEFIT:If you suffer any damage during combat, you must make a DC 15 Will save or become enraged. While enraged you suffer a -2 penalty to your Armor Class and you cannot use any Charisma-, Dexterity-, or Intelligence-based skills (except for Balance, Escape Artist, Intimidate, and Ride), the Concentration skill, or any abilities that require patience or concentration. You cannot cast spells or activate magic items that require a command word, a spell trigger (such as a wand), or spell completion (such as a scroll) to function. You can use any feat you possess except Combat Expertise, item creation feats, and metamagic feats. This enraged state lasts for a number of rounds equal to 3 + your Constitution modifier and cannot be ended prematurely. This penalty stacks with those from the use of the barbarian rage ability, resulting in a -4 AC penalty. &nl;Suggested class/race: Half-Orc
Short of Breath	KEY:Flaw ~ Short of Breath	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Con 13 or lower	DESC:You have limited stamina and you easily become exhausted by physical tasks. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Whenever you make a Strength check, a Constitution check to continue running, or use the skills Climb, Jump, or Swim, you must make a Fortitude save at the same DC as the skill or ability check. If you fail this save, you become fatigued. &nl;Normal: Doing something else that would normally cause fatigue exhausts an already fatigued character. An exhausted character suffers no further penalty by doing something else that would normally cause fatigue. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Skulker	KEY:Flaw ~ Skulker	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You are not prepared to stand face to face with your foes. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You must make a DC 15 Will save or become shaken whenever a foe engages you in melee. This penalty takes effect as soon as an enemy attacks you while you are within its threatened area. You recover from your fear as soon as you are not within an area threatened by foes. &nl;Suggested class/race: Halfling
Slow Healing	KEY:Flaw ~ Slow Healing	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	!PRESTAT:1,CON=14	DESC:You do not heal quickly. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You do not normally recover hit points or temporary ability dam-age through natural healing. If you undergo complete bed rest for a full day. you may recover either I hit point or 1 point of temporary ability dam-age. In addition, any conjuration (healing) spell cast upon you works at only half its caster level. For example, a cure moderate wounds cast upon you by an 8th-level cleric would only heal 2d8+4 points of damage, instead of 2d8+8 points of damage. &nl;Suggested class/race: Elf
Slow to Anger	KEY:Flaw ~ Slow to Anger	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Rage,TYPE.Frenzy	DESC:It takes you longer to get worked up. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Entering a rage requires a full-round action. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Solitary Paragon	KEY:Flaw ~ Solitary Paragon	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You prefer to fight alone. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1175	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPDESC:Attacking a foe you flank	BENEFIT:You gain no benefit from flanking a foe and instead suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls made against a foe you flank. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Stubby Fingers	KEY:Flaw ~ Stubby Fingers	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Dwarf%,Gnome%,Halfling%	DESC:You have short stubby fingers, which are not well-suited for grasping. [Dragon #328 (Nobody’s Perfect – New Flaws for Nonhumans)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	TEMPBONUS:PC|COMBAT|TOHIT|-4	TEMPDESC:Using a light or one-handed weapon	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on all attack rolls made when you use a light or one-handed weapon (natural weapons and unarmed attacks do not incur this penalty). in addition, you suffer a -4 penalty on all Disable Device. Open Lock, Sleight of Hand, and Use Rope checks.
Superstitious	KEY:Flaw ~ Superstitious	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Inability to cast spells	DESC:You fear magic, and avoid it when possible. [Dragon #325 (Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Whenever you see an item, effect, or location obviously created by magic (whether by spell or some other means), you become frightened. The frightened condition lasts until you can no longer see the obviously magical item, effect, or location. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Terrain Specialist	KEY:Flaw ~ Terrain Specialist	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Wild Empathy	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Track	DESC:You were trained to use your abilities in only one type of environment and are uncomfortable and less competent in all others. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Choose one terrain type (aquatic, desert, forest, hills, marsh, mountain, or plains). That is your home terrain, in which you are most comfortable. In all other terrains you suffer a -2 penalty on all wild empathy checks, as well as on Search or Survival checks made to track. You may only use your camouflage and hide in plain sight abilities in your chosen terrain. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
Test Subject	KEY:Flaw ~ Test Subject	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:You had an unscrupulous master who used you to hone his magical talents. [Dragon #333 (Class Acts – Flaws For Wizards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Choose three of the following schools: conjuration, enchantment, evocation, illusion, necromancy, and transmutation. Your saving throws made against spells and spell-like abilities from these schools suffer a -2 penalty. &nl;Suggested class/race: Wizard
Trivial Performer	KEY:Flaw ~ Trivial Performer	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Bardic Music	DESC:Your performance is lighthearted and has limited effect on others. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Bards)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:The save DC against your fascinate, suggestion, and mass suggestion abilities is half normal (rounded down). If you use the inspire courage, inspire greatness, or inspire heroics bardic music abilities. their benefits end as soon as you stop performing (rather than lasting for an additional 5 rounds). &nl;Suggested class/race: Bards
Uncontrollable Rage	KEY:Flaw ~ Uncontrollable Rage	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.Rage,TYPE.Frenzy	DESC:You have no ability to control your rage. [Dragon #325 (Class Acts - Flaws For Barbarians)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You cannot enter a rage voluntarily. If during the previous round something dealt you damage, grappled or immobilized you, or you failed a saving throw against a spell, you may enter a rage; if you do not wish to enter a rage after such an event, you must succeed at a DC 15 Will save or enter the rage involuntarily. You cannot enter a rage more times per day than you are normally entitled to. &nl;Suggested class/race: Barbarians
Warrior of the Phalanx	KEY:Flaw ~ Warrior of the Phalanx	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	DESC:Trained to fight in a group, you have difficulties when fighting alone. [Dragon #324 (Class Acts - Flaws For Paladins)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You suffer a -4 penalty on attack rolls you make when not adjacent to an ally. &nl;Suggested class/race: Paladins
Weapon Bound	KEY:Flaw ~ Weapon Bound	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRETEXT:Devotion to a specific deity	DESC:You are attuned to your deity’s weapon and no other. [Dragon #326 (Flaws For Clerics)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:You lose proficiency with all weapons except the favored weapon of your deity. This flaw does not grant you proficiency with that weapon. &nl;Suggested class/race: Cleric
Wild	KEY:Flaw ~ Wild	SORTKEY:Flaw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Flaws.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Survival=1	DESC:Accustomed only to a free life in the wild, you panic when captured or restrained. [Dragon #329 (Class Acts - Flaws For Rangers)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1176	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|1	COST:0	BENEFIT:Whenever you are entangled, pinned, or bound, you immediately become panicked. Your fear is alleviated 1 round after you are free of all bonds. Spells and effects that remove fear do not prevent this effect. &nl;Suggested class/race: Ranger
